## 4. Tier 1 completion percentage

Done ports: 3 (let, fn-call, if refactor).
Total Tier 1 ports: 14.
Completion = 3 / 14 = 0.214285714.

Tier 1 completion = 21.4%.

If we count "module on disk" as a softer success signal, the figure rises to 11 / 14 = 78.6%. The hard done number stays at 21.4% because the user-supplied done list is the only ground truth for "done".

Headline: Tier 1 is 21.4% done. Three ports lack any emit module. The next worker queue is: struct, heap, float, then a smoke script for multi, then int and match at the 256-line cap.
